--
template scope 'rebind' is ambiguous
dropped the body
--
N5008 [temp.names]/3, [temp.inst]/11: `T::template rebind<int>' names a
member class template of a completed class template instance (39 lines,
header-free, reduced from cpp17_hash_node_vector_alloc; the alias chain
mirrors libstdc++'s __uset_hashtable and the hash<vector> partial
specialization, each needed for the instantiation order).  The lookup
failed with "template scope 'rebind' is ambiguous": an error earlier in
the instance's body dropped its later members, so rebind was never
registered in the instance's scope and the fallback found every rebind of
the program.  Members after a failing one are now still registered.
